      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const items = $input.all();\nlet articleList = '';\nitems.forEach((item, i) => {\n  const j = item.json;\n  articleList += (i + 1) + '. TITLE: ' + j.title + '\\nURL: ' + j.url + '\\nSOURCE: ' + j.source + '\\nPUBLISHED: ' + j.published + '\\nSUMMARY: ' + j.description + '\\n\\n';\n});\nconst prompt = 'You are the editor of \"The Force Feed\", a daily Salesforce ecosystem newsletter. Review the following ' + items.length + ' articles collected from RSS feeds in the past 24 hours.\\n\\nYour task:\\n1. Score each article 1-10 for relevance and interest to Salesforce professionals\\n2. Assign each article one section: TOP_STORY | ECOSYSTEM_NEWS | ADMIN_DEV | APPEXCHANGE | COMMUNITY\\n3. Write a 2-sentence newsletter summary for each selected article\\n4. Select the 12-14 best articles across the sections\\n\\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON array (no markdown, no preamble) in this exact format:\\n[\\n  {\\n    \"rank\": 1,\\n    \"score\": 9,\\n    \"section\": \"TOP_STORY\",\\n    \"title\": \"Article title\",\\n    \"url\": \"Article URL\",\\n    \"source\": \"Source name\",\\n    \"summary\": \"Two sentence newsletter summary.\"\\n  }\\n]\\n\\nARTICLES:\\n' + articleList;\nreturn [{ json: { prompt } }];"
